# ============================================================
# Runtime science data
# ============================================================

# The PC Sample database - this run's session working set and the
# operator's permanent archive. Belongs to a run, not to the source
# tree. Backed up with the procedure in Documentation/OPERATIONS.md.
#
# There is no backup file beside it any more: the schema migration
# rewrites the one canonical document in place, and a *_backup.json in
# a production data folder is a second source of truth waiting to be
# read by mistake.
firmware/BD/samples/samples.json
firmware/BD/samples/.samples-*.tmp

# Downloaded source archives for DB3. 21 MB of third-party data does not
# belong in version control; DB3.json is rebuilt from it with
# py firmware/research/import_usgs.py --download
firmware/research/data/

# The consolidated calibration database IS tracked: it carries the
# protected LEGACY White/Dark that DB1 depends on. What is ignored is
# the pre-consolidation layout, so an old working tree does not
# re-commit files the migration has retired.
firmware/BD/calibration/calibration_active.json
firmware/BD/calibration/calibrations.json
firmware/BD/calibration/calibration_legacy.json
firmware/BD/calibration/acquisition_profiles.json
firmware/BD/calibration/FREYA_FULL_SPECTRAL_CAL_*.json
firmware/BD/calibration/*.tmp

# ============================================================
# Local secrets and machine-specific settings
# ============================================================

.env
.env.*
secrets.py
wifi_config.py
config.local.*
